The function `fixSpaces` processes an input string to replace any sequence of one or more consecutive whitespace characters with exactly one space. It iterates through each character in the input string, checking for spaces. When it finds a space, it checks whether there are additional consecutive spaces following it. If so, they're replaced by a single space. Otherwise, individual spaces remain untouched.

This implementation ensures that only sequences of spaces are collapsed into single spaces, preserving other characters as they are. The resulting list of strings is then joined back into a single string which is returned.

